from pathlib import Path
ROOT = Path('swarmhold_vertical_slice')
def w(rel, data):
    p=ROOT/rel; p.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True); p.write_text(data, encoding='utf-8')

w('CREDITS_ASSETS.md', '# CREDITS_ASSETS\n\n## Assets actually shipped in this vertical slice\n\nThe current source package does **not** bundle third-party art, sound or code assets. All visible OBJ meshes and WAV effects under `res://assets/` were created specifically for this vertical slice, so no external attribution is required for the files currently present in the package.\n\nThis is deliberate: the project remains self-contained and does not silently depend on assets whose binary download/import could not be runtime-verified in the build environment.\n\n### Project-created assets\n\n- `assets/models/buildings/core.obj` — Core model; created for Swarmhold; stylized low-poly sci-fi.\n- `assets/models/buildings/wall.obj` — wall model; created for Swarmhold.\n- `assets/models/buildings/turret_base.obj` / `turret_head.obj` — Autocannon base and rotating head; created for Swarmhold.\n- `assets/models/buildings/extractor.obj` — Extractor model; created for Swarmhold.\n- `assets/models/buildings/storage.obj` — Storage model; created for Swarmhold.\n- `assets/models/enemies/bug_body.obj` / `bug_leg.obj` — Swarmer body/leg geometry; created for Swarmhold.\n- `assets/models/environment/terrain.obj` / `rock.obj` — arena and rock geometry; created for Swarmhold.\n- `assets/models/resources/biomass_node.obj` / `crystal_cluster.obj` — resource geometry; created for Swarmhold.\n- `assets/audio/build.wav`, `shot.wav`, `alert.wav`, `hit.wav` — synthesized specifically for Swarmhold.\n\n## Vetted third-party candidates — NOT bundled yet\n\nThese were researched and license-checked for the next art replacement/polish pass. They are listed here so later imports remain traceable. Their absence from this package means they do not create a current attribution obligation.\n\n| Candidate | Author/source | License | Intended use | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Ultimate Monsters | Quaternius | CC0 | animated insect/alien enemy candidates, including Armabee | Approved candidate; not bundled |\n| Modular Sci-Fi MegaKit | Quaternius | CC0 | Core, walls, industrial sci-fi modules/props | Approved candidate; not bundled |\n| Sci-Fi Essentials Kit | Quaternius | CC0 | turrets/robots/props/VFX-compatible sci-fi pieces | Approved candidate; not bundled |\n| Stylized Nature MegaKit | Quaternius | CC0 | rocks and environment dressing | Approved candidate; not bundled |\n| Cyberpunk Game Kit | Quaternius | CC0 | turret/mechanical alternatives | Approved candidate; not bundled |\n| Modular Space Kit | Kenney | CC0 | modular base pieces | Approved candidate; not bundled |\n| Space Station Kit | Kenney | CC0 | base/industrial station props | Approved candidate; not bundled |\n| Spider (3D, animated) | br-n518 / OpenGameArt | CC0 | extremely light animated insect fallback | Approved candidate; not bundled |\n\n### Sources\n\n- Quaternius Ultimate Monsters: https://quaternius.com/packs/ultimatemonsters.html\n- Quaternius Modular Sci-Fi MegaKit: https://quaternius.com/packs/modularscifimegakit.html\n- Quaternius Sci-Fi Essentials Kit: https://quaternius.com/packs/scifiessentialskit.html\n- Quaternius Stylized Nature MegaKit: https://quaternius.com/packs/stylizednaturemegakit.html\n- Quaternius Cyberpunk Game Kit: https://quaternius.com/packs/cyberpunkgamekit.html\n- Kenney Modular Space Kit: https://kenney.nl/assets/modular-space-kit\n- Kenney Space Station Kit: https://kenney.nl/assets/space-station-kit\n- OpenGameArt Spider: https://opengameart.org/content/spider-2\n\nWhen any candidate is actually imported, add exact filename/version, direct source, license, author attribution requirements and all project modifications to this file before release.\n')
